  "summary": "Install-time host reconnaissance beacon to hardcoded remote endpoint",
  "details": "setup.py installs a custom cmdclass (PostInstallCommand) that runs automatically during `pip install`. The hook collects hostname, uid, cwd, pid, and the full list of environment variable KEYS from the installer machine, serializes them as JSON, and POSTs them via urllib.request.urlopen to the hardcoded endpoint https://5h6gijnewx787zu6.ixx.sh. The callback is unconditional, unauthenticated, and requires no user opt-in; installing the package causes the installer host's identity and environment metadata to be sent to an author-controlled remote server. The package name self-labels as an 'rce-test', but the code performs an unsolicited install-time exfiltration beacon regardless of that label.",
